{
  "description" : "Byte layouts signed or MACed between the iOS client and StealthRelay. Integers are big-endian; pool_id is the 16 raw UUID bytes (RFC 4122 order).",
  "format" : "relay-transcripts",
  "notes" : [
    "Ed25519 signatures from CryptoKit are randomised: signature_hex verifies under ed25519_public_hex but is not reproducible. Verify, never compare.",
    "PoW hash is SHA-256 on BOTH sides: Swift WebSocketTransport.solvePoW and Rust stealthos-crypto pow_hash (the Rust module doc comment still says BLAKE2b-256; the code uses sha2::Sha256).",
    "The Swift solver accepts any challenge length and any difficulty 0-255; the Rust side issues 32-byte challenges. A difficulty above what SHA-256 output can satisfy makes the Swift solver loop forever.",
    "The invite HKDF salt is the raw pool_id; info is the ASCII label immediately followed by the raw 16-byte token id. Rust additionally publishes commitment = BLAKE2b-256(vk), which the client never computes.",
    "host_auth appends the server nonce bytes exactly as decoded from base64 (any length)."
  ],
  "schema_version" : 1,
  "sources" : [
    "LocalPackages/ConnectionPool/Sources/Transport/WebSocketTransport.swift",
